{
  "summary": "The UI largely matches the design spec—most screens, states, messages, navigation, and layout pass the automated headless audits (axe=0 violations, Lighthouse accessibility 100, best‑practices 100, flow OK). However, a few critical gaps were found that would break the primary flow or cause accessibility regressions if left unaddressed. These revolve around missing required copy, inconsistent use of design tokens, focus visibility, and sign‑up/sign‑in best‑practice details.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignUpScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The **Create account** loading state displays a generic spinner overlay but the required overlay text **“Creating account…”** is missing. The design spec also mandates that fields be disabled during loading.",
      "fix": "Add a `<Text>` element with the exact message \"Creating account…\" inside the loading overlay and ensure all input components receive the `disabled` prop when the loading flag is true."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignInScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Sign‑in submission error shows a generic toast but the exact message **“Incorrect email or password.”** is not used; instead a generic \"Login failed\" is rendered. This violates the spec and could break UI tests that look for the exact string.",
      "fix": "Replace the generic error toast message with the exact copy from the spec: `\"Incorrect email or password.\"` and ensure the toast uses the error styling (`background: var(--color-error)`, `color: var(--color-on-error)`)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/DashboardScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The empty state banner uses the title **\"No data yet\"** but the body copy is **\"You haven’t added any receipts or mileage yet. Tap the + button to get started.\"** instead of the spec‑required body **\"Add receipts or mileage to see your financial summary.\"** This mismatch leads to failing automated UI‑test expectations.",
      "fix": "Update the empty‑state component to use the exact body text from the spec. Verify that the primary CTA button label is **\"Add first receipt\"** and that it triggers navigation to the receipt capture screen."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/FormField.tsx",
      "issue": "Form fields use placeholders as the sole label (e.g., \"e.g., 45.67\") which violates sign‑up/sign‑in best practice that requires visible labels above each field. Also, `autoComplete` attributes are not set, preventing autofill on mobile browsers.",
      "fix": "Add a `<Text>` label component above each `TextInput` using the `label` prop. Pass appropriate `autoComplete` values (e.g., `email`, `new-password`) to the inputs. Ensure the label is linked to the input via `accessibilityLabel`/`nativeID` for screen readers."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "The button component does not render a visible focus ring when navigated via keyboard (no `focusVisible` style). This fails the accessibility requirement for a 2 px solid primary outline on focus.",
      "fix": "Add a `style` that applies `borderWidth: 2, borderColor: theme.colors.primary` when the button receives focus (use `onFocus` + state or `useFocusRing` from `react-native-paper`). Ensure the focus ring meets the 44×44 px target size."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/SummaryCard.tsx",
      "issue": "Card elevation uses a hard‑coded shadow value (`elevation: 4`) instead of the design token `elevation.card`. This creates visual inconsistency and deviates from the token‑driven design system.",
      "fix": "Replace the hard‑coded elevation with the token value from `theme.elevation.card`. Import the theme and spread `...theme.elevation.card` into the card style."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/ReceiptCaptureScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "After a successful receipt save, the UI shows a toast but does not navigate back to the dashboard nor refresh the receipt list. The spec expects the new receipt to appear instantly in the list.",
      "fix": "After displaying the success toast, programmatically navigate back to the dashboard (or use a context/state update) and trigger a data refetch to update the receipt list."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/ExportScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Export error toast displays generic text **\"Export failed.\"** rather than the required **\"Export failed. Please try again.\"**. Also, the offline banner text is missing the required copy **\"Cannot export while offline.\"**.",
      "fix": "Update error and offline messages to match the spec exactly. Ensure the offline banner appears with correct styling (`background: var(--color-error)`, `color: var(--color-on-error)`)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/Screen.tsx",
      "issue": "The `Screen` wrapper sets `maxWidth: 360` via inline style but does not use the design token `spacing.lg` for horizontal padding. This violates the rule that all spacing must come from the token system.",
      "fix": "Replace the hard‑coded padding with `paddingHorizontal: theme.spacing.lg` and import the theme where the component is defined."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/navigation/index.tsx",
      "issue": "Bottom tab bar navigation does not expose the `accessibilityRole=\"tablist\"` and each tab button lacks `accessibilityState={{ selected }}` and a 2 px focus outline, breaking keyboard navigation on web.",
      "fix": "Add `role=\"tablist\"` to the `BottomNavigation` container. For each tab item, set `accessibilityRole=\"tab\"`, `accessibilityState={{ selected: isFocused }}`, and a focus‑visible style (`borderWidth: 2, borderColor: theme.colors.primary`)."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/EmptyState.tsx",
      "issue": "The CTA button inside the empty state uses a custom class name (`empty-cta`) without any associated CSS, resulting in missing styling on some platforms.",
      "fix": "Replace the custom class with the existing `PrimaryButton` component which already applies the design token styles. Remove the unused class name."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/MileageEntryScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Mileage entry form fields lack the `keyboardType=\"numeric\"` attribute on the miles input, making it hard to enter numbers on mobile keyboards.",
      "fix": "Add `keyboardType=\"numeric\"` (or `number-pad`) to the miles input field and set `inputMode=\"numeric\"` for web accessibility."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Button hover state is not defined for web; the spec expects a visual change on hover (e.g., darker background).",
      "fix": "Add a CSS rule for `:hover` that sets `background-color: var(--color-primary-variant)` while preserving the `onPrimary` text color."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/FormField.tsx",
      "issue": "Error state only changes the underline colour but does not display the required inline error text when `error` prop is true.",
      "fix": "Render a `<HelperText type=\"error\">` component below the `TextInput` with the exact error message passed from the screen."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/Screen.tsx",
      "issue": "Screen does not respect safe‑area insets on iOS (no `SafeAreaView` wrapper), which could cause content to be clipped by the notch or home indicator.",
      "fix": "Wrap the root view of each screen in `<SafeAreaView edges={['top', 'bottom']} style={{ flex: 1 }}>` and ensure the `Screen` component propagates the safe area padding."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "The button’s minimum width is enforced via a flex style (`minWidth: 120`) but the component does not enforce the minimum height of 48 px on all platforms, causing a smaller tap target on web.",
      "fix": "Explicitly set `height: 48` and `minHeight: 48` via the `contentStyle` prop of the Paper `Button` component."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/LoadingOverlay.tsx",
      "issue": "Loading overlay uses a semi‑transparent background color expressed as a hex value (`#00000080`) instead of the design token `color-on-surface` with opacity. This could cause colour inconsistencies in dark mode.",
      "fix": "Replace the hard‑coded overlay colour with `rgba(${theme.colors.onSurface}, 0.5)` derived from the token."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/Screen.tsx",
      "issue": "The `maxWidth: 360` is hard‑coded rather than using the CSS custom property `--space-xxl` (or a dedicated width token).",
      "fix": "Define a CSS custom property for the max content width (`--max-content-width: 360px`) in the theme and apply it instead of a magic number."
    }
  ]
}

