{
  "summary": "The app passes the automated accessibility checks (axe, Lighthouse) and the primary flow runs without crashing, but a closer, spec‑level review uncovers several gaps that affect user experience and design fidelity. Key issues include missing or incomplete UI states (Dashboard empty state, receipt‑capture permission flow), inconsistent use of the design‑token theme (hard‑coded colors, sizes, and elevations), absent best‑practice features on the auth screens (password show/hide toggle, explicit autocomplete attributes, proper field‑level error linking), lack of a visible focus indicator for keyboard navigation, and occasional styling patterns (className without a CSS rule) that are not backed by the token system. While none of these break the core functionality, they impede the polished product experience expected by the spec and can cause accessibility regressions for power‑users or keyboard‑only users. The findings below detail each problem and prescribe concrete fixes.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/DashboardScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Empty‑state UI is missing the required CTA \"Add first receipt\" and the exact copy \"You haven’t added any receipts or mileage yet. Tap the + button to get started.\" When the user has no data the screen shows only a spinner or a blank list, leaving the user without a forward path.",
      "fix": "Add an EmptyState component that uses the design tokens (background, spacing, typography) and includes the title \"No data yet\", the body text, and a PrimaryButton with label \"Add first receipt\". Ensure the button navigates to the receipt capture screen."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/ReceiptCaptureScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The permission‑prompt modal does not display the exact copy \"FinanceMate needs camera access to photograph receipts.\" and the denial notice with \"Camera access denied. You can select a photo from your library.\". Also the \"Choose from library\" button is missing when the user denies camera permission.",
      "fix": "Create a Modal component that pulls its text from constants matching the spec. Use the PrimaryButton with label \"Allow\" and a TextLink for \"Deny\". When denied, render a notice view with a TextLink labeled \"Choose from library\" that triggers the image picker."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/navigation/index.tsx",
      "issue": "The BottomTabBar (persistent navigation) is omitted from the MileageEntryScreen and ExportScreen, so users cannot navigate to other primary actions without using the back button.",
      "fix": "Wrap all signed‑in screens (Dashboard, MileageEntry, Export, Settings) in a TabNavigator that always renders the BottomNavigation component. Ensure the tab bar is hidden only on web when the navigation drawer is active."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignUpScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Password field lacks a show/hide toggle and the live rule list is not rendered. This violates the spec’s sign‑up best practices and can cause user frustration.",
      "fix": "Enhance the FormField wrapper to accept a `right` prop with a `IconButton` that toggles `secureTextEntry`. Add a `HelperText` that updates live as the user types, displaying the exact rule text \"12 + characters, uppercase, lowercase, number, symbol\"."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignInScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Submit button can be tapped repeatedly during loading because it is not disabled; fields are not disabled either, potentially causing duplicate login attempts.",
      "fix": "During the loading state set `disabled={true}` on all inputs and the PrimaryButton, and render the overlay spinner with the message \"Signing you in…\". Re‑enable after the API response."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Button styling uses hard‑coded hex colors (`backgroundColor: '#0066FF'`) instead of the theme tokens (`theme.colors.primary`). This breaks the design‑token consistency and makes future theming difficult.",
      "fix": "Replace all literal color values with `theme.colors.primary` and `theme.colors.onPrimary`. Use `theme.roundness` for borderRadius and `theme.spacing.lg` for padding/margin."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/FormField.tsx",
      "issue": "TextInput components lack `autoComplete` / `textContentType` props for email and password fields, missing an important accessibility and UX enhancement.",
      "fix": "Add `autoComplete='email'` and `keyboardType='email-address'` to the email field, and `autoComplete='current-password'` / `textContentType='password'` to the password field. Ensure the password field also has `importantForAutofill='yes'` on Android."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/FormField.tsx",
      "issue": "Field‑level error messages are rendered with `HelperText` but are not linked to the associated input via `accessibilityDescribedBy`, reducing screen‑reader usability.",
      "fix": "Assign each input a unique nativeID and pass that ID to the `HelperText` via `accessibilityDescribedBy`. When an error is present, focus the first invalid field programmatically."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/Screen.tsx",
      "issue": "Screen wrapper uses a fixed `padding: 16` style instead of the token‑based spacing (`theme.spacing.lg`). This results in inconsistent margins across components.",
      "fix": "Refactor the Screen component to pull spacing from the theme: `paddingHorizontal: theme.spacing.lg`, `paddingVertical: theme.spacing.lg`. Ensure maxWidth is set to `theme.spacing.xxxl` (360 px)."
