{
  "summary": "The UI implementation largely follows the DESIGN.md spec – all screens appear in the navigation flow, the major states (default, loading, error, empty) are present, and the aXe audit reports zero accessibility violations. However, several user‑experience and implementation gaps break the spec’s best‑practice expectations and cause a noticeably low performance score. The most critical problems are missing offline handling on the Export screen (leaving a state unhandled) and incomplete sign‑up UX (no live password rule list, missing show/hide toggle, and missing autofill attributes). Medium‑severity issues include missing focus‑visible outlines, hard‑coded style values, and bundled image assets that bloat the bundle. Dependency warnings also need addressing.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/ExportScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "The Export screen does not render the “Offline” banner (\"Cannot export while offline.\") nor disable the Export buttons when NetInfo reports offline, leaving the offline state unhandled and allowing a failing API call.",
      "fix": "Import NetInfo, watch the connectivity status, render the offline banner when offline, and set the Export CSV/PDF buttons to disabled with a spinner overlay. Also announce the banner via an ARIA live region."
    },
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "file": "expo-app/src/screens/SignUpScreen.tsx",
      "issue": "Sign‑up form lacks the live password‑rule helper list defined in the spec and does not provide a show/hide password toggle, making it impossible for users to see password requirements or verify entry.",
      "fix": "Add a component below the password field that updates in real time with the rule list (length, upper‑case, lower‑case, number, symbol). Include an eye icon button in the TextInput’s right slot that toggles `secureTextEntry` and set `autoComplete=\"new-password\"`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/FormField.tsx",
      "issue": "Form fields use raw numeric height (`height: 48`) and padding instead of the design‑token values (`theme.spacing.md`, `theme.roundness`).",
      "fix": "Replace hard‑coded numbers with `theme.spacing.md` for vertical spacing and `theme.roundness` for border radius. Import the theme token values and apply them to the TextInput style."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "Button does not expose a visible focus ring on web; keyboard users cannot see which element is focused, violating WCAG 2.4.7.",
      "fix": "Add a `:focus-visible` style (or use the `onFocus` prop) that applies a `2px solid var(--color-primary)` outline. Ensure the outline respects the 44×44 px touch target minimum."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/Screen.tsx",
      "issue": "Screen wrapper sets `paddingHorizontal: 16` directly, bypassing the global max‑content width of 360 px and the 4/8 px grid defined in the design tokens.",
      "fix": "Replace the hard‑coded padding with `theme.spacing.lg` and use `maxWidth: 360` (or the CSS custom property `--space-xl`) to enforce the content width. Center the container with `alignSelf: 'center'`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/Header.tsx",
      "issue": "Header lacks proper ARIA landmarks (`role=\"banner\"`) and the app title is rendered with a generic `<Text>` without `accessibilityRole=\"header\"` and level.",
      "fix": "Add `accessibilityRole=\"banner\"` to the Appbar component and wrap the title in `<Text accessibilityRole=\"header\" accessibilityLevel={1}>`. Ensure the settings icon button has `accessibilityLabel=\"Settings\"`."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/EmptyState.tsx",
      "issue": "Illustration image uses a fixed width/height and no `accessibilityLabel`, potentially causing layout overflow on small screens and missing alt text.",
      "fix": "Make the image responsive (`width: '100%', maxWidth: 340`) and add `accessibilityLabel=\"No data illustration\" accessible={false}` or appropriate labeling for decorative images."
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "file": "expo-app/package.json",
      "issue": "Medium‑severity vulnerabilities in bundled dependencies: `decode-uri-component` (CVE‑2026‑45822), `sprintf-js` (CVE‑2026‑97058), and `uuid` (CVE‑2026‑41907).",
      "fix": "Upgrade `decode-uri-component` to >=0.5.0, replace `sprintf-js` with native template literals or a maintained alternative, and upgrade `uuid` to >=11.1.1. Run `npm audit fix` and verify no new issues."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/PrimaryButton.tsx",
      "issue": "The component uses a `className=\"primary-button\"` prop on the RN Paper Button but no corresponding CSS class is defined for the web build, leaving unused class names.",
      "fix": "Remove the unused `className` attribute or create a matching CSS rule in `web/theme.css` that forwards to the token colors and spacing."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "file": "expo-app/src/components/ui/Screen.tsx",
      "issue": "Missing `role=\"main\"` on the top‑level screen view for proper landmark navigation on the web.",
      "fix": "Add `role=\"main\"` to the wrapper `<View>` (or `<SafeAreaView>`) and ensure it is not hidden with `accessibilityElementsHidden`."
    }
  ]
}

